  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best-performing configuration is config_033 (SCVI_n200 + ResNet50, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) at 0.713 acc / 0.695 F1. Image-only ResNet50 is very weak (0.208), yet adding it to the multimodal pipeline yields a meaningful +0.06 gain over RNA-only (0.653→0.713). Weighted fusion clearly outperforms concat (0.713 vs 0.688), and transformer aggregation is the established choice. Uncertainty: We have only tested one image encoder (ResNet50). It is unknown whether a stronger pretrained encoder (ImageNet ViT-L) would extract more useful visual signal and further improve multimodal performance, or whether the image contribution is inherently limited. This experiment (config_039) changes exactly one variable—ResNet50→ViT-L—while holding the rest of the best configuration (SCVI_n200, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) constant. It directly tests whether image encoder quality is a bottleneck, which is a critical architectural decision. If ViT-L improves performance, it validates investing in stronger visual representations; if not, it indicates the image modality's contribution is saturated and further effort should focus on RNA-side improvements. This single-variable comparison is the most informative next step under a limited budget."
}

